# 13247: Dial: Invalid From number (caller ID)

Positive FeedbackNegative Feedback

* * *

* * *

## ERROR: 13247

[error-13247 page anchor](https://www.twilio.com/docs/api/errors/13247#error-13247)

Positive FeedbackNegative Feedback

PROGRAMMABLE VOICE

ERROR

* * *

## Description

[description page anchor](https://www.twilio.com/docs/api/errors/13247#description)

Positive FeedbackNegative Feedback

You attempted to initiate an outbound phone call or message, but the `From` parameter you supplied was not a valid phone number or alphanumeric sender ID.

Twilio accepts phone numbers in [E.164 format](https://www.twilio.com/docs/glossary/what-e164 "E.164 format") (i.e. "+1 format"), 10-digit US and Canadian numbers with any combination of non-digit separators, or Alphanumeric Sender IDs (SMS only) with up to 11 alphanumeric characters \[a-zA-Z0-9\]. Refer to [this page(link takes you to an external page)](https://support.twilio.com/hc/en-us/articles/223133867-Using-Alphanumeric-Sender-ID-with-Messaging-Services "this page") for acceptable characters.

The number must not be on a do-not-originate (DNO) list, and Alpha Sender IDs may not be generic.

### Possible Causes

[possible-causes page anchor](https://www.twilio.com/docs/api/errors/13247#possible-causes)

Positive FeedbackNegative Feedback

- You have supplied a phone number that was not in [E.164 format](https://www.twilio.com/docs/glossary/what-e164 "E.164 format")
- Your `From` phone number is on a do-not-originate (DNO) list

### Possible Solutions

[possible-solutions page anchor](https://www.twilio.com/docs/api/errors/13247#possible-solutions)

Positive FeedbackNegative Feedback

- Ensure your number is formatted in [E.164 format](https://www.twilio.com/docs/glossary/what-e164 "E.164 format")
- Ensure that your `From` number is assigned and not on a do-not-originate (DNO) list.

