* * *

## Error - 20154

[error---20154 page anchor](https://www.twilio.com/docs/api/errors/20154#error---20154)

Positive FeedbackNegative Feedback

### Invalid Claim Set

[invalid-claim-set page anchor](https://www.twilio.com/docs/api/errors/20154#invalid-claim-set)

Positive FeedbackNegative Feedback

The JWT could be parsed, but the claims in the payload section are invalid.

#### Possible Causes

[possible-causes page anchor](https://www.twilio.com/docs/api/errors/20154#possible-causes)

- One of the required claims is missing.

- For JWTs used as part of Public Key Client Validation, we require two custom claims:
- "hrh" - HTTP headers that were included when calculating the request hash
- "rqh" - The hash of the HTTP request

#### Possible Solution:

[possible-solution page anchor](https://www.twilio.com/docs/api/errors/20154#possible-solution)

- Make sure you are using the latest Twilio Helper Library
- For the details on JWTs used as part of Public Key Client Validation, see [the documentation](https://www.twilio.com/docs/api/credentials/public-key-client-validation-getting-started "the documentation")
- To check whether the JWT is structurally correct, you can use the tools available at jwt.io.

