## RCS FAQs

### How to switch from SMS to RCS?

An icon of a plus symbolAn icon of a minus symbol

Twilio customers can go directly to the Twilio Console and begin building and testing with RCS today! [Log in to get started](https://console.twilio.com/us1/develop/rcs/overview).

### What is the difference between SMS vs. RCS?

An icon of a plus symbolAn icon of a minus symbol

RCS enhances traditional SMS by supporting features like branded & verified sender IDs, rich media, and interactive content, providing a more engaging and interactive messaging experience for consumers.

### Where is RCS Business messaging available?

An icon of a plus symbolAn icon of a minus symbol

Google has partnered with major mobile carriers to bring full RCS coverage to [many countries around the world](https://www.twilio.com/docs/rcs/regional)—and support is growing all the time.

### What devices support RCS?

An icon of a plus symbolAn icon of a minus symbol

RCS is currently available on all Android devices and Apple devices for consumers upgraded to iOS 18.1 or above (released in 2024). Currently, 23+ countries have RCS Business Messaging enabled for their customers.

### What features are included in RCS?

An icon of a plus symbolAn icon of a minus symbol

The RCS Business Messaging channel includes branded, verified senders; rich content like media, cards, and buttons; as well as additional data, including delivery and read receipts.\*

### What if I message a user without RCS Business messaging?

An icon of a plus symbolAn icon of a minus symbol

If the recipient’s device does not support RCS Business Messaging, the message will be delivered as a standard SMS or MMS.

### Is RCS Business Messaging secure?

An icon of a plus symbolAn icon of a minus symbol

Yes. RCS offers more security features than traditional SMS. Messages are transmitted over the internet and are encrypted in transit, providing better protection against interception and unauthorized access. This makes RCS a more secure option for businesses looking to engage with customers.

### What can my business do with RCS?

An icon of a plus symbolAn icon of a minus symbol

Create more engaging and interactive conversations with your customers through rich multimedia (images, videos), interactive buttons, carousels, and branded messaging. These enhanced capabilities significantly improve customer engagement, boost brand visibility, and drive higher conversion rates. [Get started with RCS and Twilio](https://www.twilio.com/en-us/blog/get-started-rcs-twilio)

